Across history, it was extremely rare to encounter a Powerbonded Titan. {{Source|Cave of the Casterwills}} In the modern age, knowledge of the Powerbond was widespread amongst Seekers including [[Nimue Casterwill]] {{Source|S2E29}}, [[Dante Vale]] {{Source|S2E27}}, and [[Tantras]] who knew that the mechanics of its power and abilities were not to be underestimated. {{Source|S2E36}}

At some point in the 16th century, [[Nostradamus]] formed a Powerbond with his Titan, [[Sorcerel]]. [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] encountered her when they were sent back in time by [[Kronos]] and fought with Nostradamus and [[Viktor Casterwill]]. Sophie, who had acquired the same Sorcerel herself but centuries later, was surprised to see a Powerbonded version of her. {{Source|HM17}}

[[File:S2E27 Lok Kipperin summon 2.png|thumb|Lok fuses with [[Kipperin|Powerbonded Kipperin]] for the first time]]
[[Lok Lambert]] first discovered the Powerbond power while searching for his father’s last known whereabouts in [[Peru]], a mission of significant emotional importance to him. Upon summoning [[Kipperin]], he was surprised to find that the Titan had drastically changed upon invocation, merging with him to form one body. [[Dante Vale]] then explained that, because his bond to his father's Titan was so strong, they had become Powerbonded. Later, Lok Powerbonded with [[Baselaird]], to save Dante and Zhalia from [[Wilder]] and [[The Organization]]. {{Source|S2E27}}

In the [[Crystal Caves]], [[Sophie Casterwill]] was able to empower and invoke the spirit of [[Sabriel]] despite Sabriel’s Amulet having been destroyed. This was made possible in part by the presence of [[Sorcerel]], Sabriel’s sister and a kindred spirit, who was resting within the Crystal Caves and with whom Sophie was actively attempting to form a bond. Through this connection, Sophie was able to reestablish a connection  with Sabriel’s spirit and Powerbond with her, bypassing the traditional requirement of an Amulet. Throughout these events, residual energy associated with Sabriel was shown lingering around Sophie’s hand within the caves, indicating an ongoing connection that ultimately culminated in the formation of the Powerbond. {{Source|S2E29}}

[[Dante Vale]] invoked the Powerbond with [[Caliban]] in a last effort to save himself from [[Rassimov]] and the [[Blood Spiral]] in [[Klaus' bookshop]], with Powerbonded Caliban’s martial arts abilities helping to even the battle and give the team an opportunity to escape. {{Source|S2E32}}
[[File:S2E34 Arc vs Lok.png|thumb|Lok powerbonds with [[Lindorm]] while under attack from [[Arc]]]]
In order to protect Lok from the [[Legendary Titan]] of Fate, [[Arc]], [[Lindorm]] became Powerbonded with him. {{Source|S2E34}} 

When [[Zhalia Moon]] was discovered infiltrating the [[Blood Spiral]] by [[Tantras]], [[Gareon]] became Powerbonded with her and used his Scramblemind ability to erase Tantras’ memory of her being a double agent. {{Source|S2E39}}

When [[Sophie Casterwill]] was fighting against [[Kiel]] at the [[Fortress of Iron Will]], she [[Powerbonded]] with Sorcerel, thus regaining her strength to fight Kiel. {{Source|S2E40}}

When the [[Blood Spiral]] travelled to the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]], Harrison Fears managed to bond with the vampiric [[Antedeluvian]] and then Powerbond with him, at an exceptionally rapid pace. {{Source|S2E43}} 
[[File:S2E43 Antedleuvian Kaioh Life Drain.png|thumb|Powerbonded Antedeluvian uses his Life Drain ability on [[Kaioh the Tracker]]]]

[[Breaker]] became Powerbonded to Grier during a battle in [[the Professor's castle]] in order to save him from asphyxiation at the hands [[Wilder|Wilder's]] [[Grand Façade]], much to the amazement of [[Den Fears]]. Powerbonded Breaker then defeated Grand Façade with his "Crushing Grip" power. {{Source|S2E46}}

In [[Egypt]], Dante became Powerbonded to [[Ariel]] while under attack from [[Rassimov]] and the Legendary Titan of War, [[Legion]]. Dante intended for Ariel to get his team to safety, while he led Rassimov away with the [[Necklace of Tutankhamun]]. However, [[Solwing]] snatched the Necklace himself, leading Rassimov and Legion away and saving Dante. Powerbonded Ariel stopped Dante from going after him and reminded him to save the team. {{Source|S2E47}}
[[File:S2E52 Lok Pendragon.png|thumb|Lok's Powerbond with [[Pendragon]], the first known Legendary Titan to Powerbond]]
At the [[Blood Spiral Base]], after faltering during his final battle with his brother, Harrison, [[Den Fears]] sensed Vigilante becoming Powerbonded, reminding him that him not to let his friends down. After invoking Powerbonded Vigilante, Den merged with him using his new "Cindercloak" ability and fought and defeated Powerbonded Antedeluvian. Before he could defeat Harrison however, Vigilante was disrupted by falling rocks and sent back to his Amulet. {{Source|S2E51}}

During the final battle with [[the Betrayer]], Pendragon's Amulet independently emerged from the Willblade to save Lok from [[Demigorgan]], the Titan of Betrayal. Pendragon was then revealed to have become Powerbonded, defeating the Titan copies of [[Sabriel]], [[Raijin]] and [[Gareon]] created by Demigorgan. {{Source|S2E52}}

[[File:S2E47 Sophie Sabriel icon.png|thumb|Sophie's Powerbond with [[Sabriel]] means she can be summoned from her hand]]
In exceptional circumstances, the Powerbond can bypass the requirement of an [[Amulet]], seen in the case of [[Sabriel]] whose bond with [[Sophie Casterwill]] was so strong that, despite her Amulet being destroyed, Sophie was able to reestablish a connection with Sabriel’s spirit and Powerbond with her, now summoning her from her hand. This anomaly was made possible in part by the presence of [[Sorcerel]], Sabriel’s sister, who was resting within the [[Crystal Caves]] and with whom Sophie was actively attempting to form a bond. {{Source|S2E29}} 

The formation of a Powerbond may also occur far more rapidly in rare cases of extreme compatibility. [[Harrison Fears]] summoned [[Antedeluvian]] in his Powerbonded form only shortly after acquiring his Amulet, suggesting that a Powerbond can be established almost instantaneously when a Seeker’s disposition significantly aligns with a Titan’s nature, particularly where a Seeker’s personality is similar to a Titan’s previous Seeker, as Harrison was to [[Vlad Dracul]]. {{Source|S2E43}}

[[File:S2E34 Powerbonded Lindorm Lok.png|thumb|[[Lindorm|Powerbonded Lindorm]] gains an additional pair of arms and a second tail]]
Upon their transformation, Powerbonded Titans typically gain golden or gilded armor, often covering areas that were previously unarmoured or less defined. This is frequently accompanied by an increased physical stature, with some Titans appearing larger or more imposing than their original forms, seen significantly in the cases of [[Baselaird]] and [[Gareon]]. {{Source|S2E39}} Another defining feature is the appearance of a gem embedded in the centre of the chest, {{Source|Doorway to Huntik}} which visually corresponds to gem on the Titan's Amulet, which itself signifies their Titan type. {{Source|Huntik.com}} In some cases, the Powerbond can result in more dramatic anatomical changes. [[Lindorm]] developed an additional pair of arms and a second tail, increasing his total number of limbs and altering his physical form. {{source|S2E34}}

A Powerbond also establishes an exceptionally strong empathic link between the Seeker and Titan. As a result, when a Seeker is injured, their Powerbonded Titan may experience or react to the Seeker’s pain, reflecting the depth of their synchronization. This effect was seen when [[Lok Lambert]] was struck by a [[Poisonfang]] power, with his Titan [[Baselaird]] also experiencing the effects and becoming temporarily stunned. {{Source|S2E28}}

[[File:S2E35 Dante Caliban punch Suit Myrmidon.png|thumb|Dante and Powerbonded Caliban use "Mirror Fight" to take down [[Myrmidon]] and a [[Suit]] in perfect sync]]
Powerbonded Titans display significantly enhanced combat skills, including increased offensive and defensive capabilities, as well as the manifestation of new abilities made possible through heightened mental and physical synchronization with their Seeker. These abilities are typically in direct coordination with the Powerbonded Titan, as demonstrated by [[Dante Vale]] and [[Caliban]]’s "Mirror Fight", [[Zhalia Moon]] and [[Gareon]]’s "Scramblemind", and [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Lindorm]]’s "Spinnerslash". {{Source|S2E36}} 

Powerbonded Titans are composed of a distinct form of Powerbonded energy. In the case of [[Baselaird]], this energy could be transferred to his Seeker, allowing [[Lok Lambert]] to enhance his own abilities through the technique known as "Focus Blade". {{Source|S2E45}}  

In some cases, Powerbonding enables a Titan and Seeker to temporarily merge into a single combined entity, acting as one both physically and mentally. This was demonstrated by [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Kipperin]] with the "Winged Fusion" ability {{Source|S2E27}} as well as [[Den Fears]] and [[Vigilante]] through the "Cindercloak" ability, representing most extreme manifestations of Seeker–Titan synchronization. {{Source|S2E51}}

